.TH LIR-NODE 1 2026-11-23 Lir "Lir"
.SH NAME
lir-node \- one node of Lir, a clustered MQTT broker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lir-node
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR path ]
.RI [ settings ]
.br
.B lir-node
.B \-\-version
.br
.B lir-node
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lir-node
runs one node of Lir: a Dannan node that serves MQTT 5.0, 3.1.1 and 3.1 over
TCP, and over TLS and WebSocket when configured. Every node of a cluster is
the same; a client may connect to any of them, and what it publishes reaches
the subscribers on every node. Each node says where it serves in Dannan's
roster, where clients and the other nodes find it.
.PP
It runs until SIGTERM or SIGINT, then withdraws what it advertises, closes
its clients and leaves the cluster.
.SH SETTINGS
Settings come from, each overriding the one before: the defaults, the YAML
file
.RB ( \-\-config ,
.BR $LIR_CONFIG ,
else
.I /etc/lir/config.yaml
when it exists),
.I secrets.yaml
beside it, the environment
.RB ( LIR_ *),
then the command line. A key is a flag and a variable by one rule:
.B cluster.listen.port
is
.B \-\-cluster\-listen\-port
and
.BR LIR_CLUSTER_LISTEN_PORT .
.B \-\-help
lists every setting.
.TP
.B cluster.*
The node in Dannan's cluster, shared by every node binary of the stack:
.BR cluster.key ,
.BR cluster.bootstrap ,
.BR cluster.state ,
.BR cluster.listen.port
and the rest. A node needs a state directory and the cluster's key (or a
certificate).
.TP
.BR mqtt ", " mqtts ", " ws ", " wss
Where clients reach it, each listener named as every node program of the
stack names its own:
.IB name .listen.address\fR,
.IB name .listen.port\fR,
.IB name .tls.certificate\fR,
.IB name .tls.key
and
.IB name .tls.ca\fR.
.B mqtt
(1883) is always served;
.B mqtts
(8883) and
.B wss
(8443) when given their pair;
.B ws
(8080) when given a port. Also
.BR mqtt.advertise ,
.BR mqtt.client_certificates ,
.B mqtt.maximum_packet_size
and
.BR mqtt.topic_alias_maximum .
.TP
.B anonymous.*
Clients that sign in with nothing are refused unless
.B anonymous.allow
is set, and are then held to the topic filters in
.BR anonymous.publish ,
.B anonymous.retain
and
.BR anonymous.subscribe .
.TP
.B lugh.*
With the Lugh plugin: the issuers whose access tokens sign clients in, and
the audience a token must name.
.TP
.BR log.* ", " node.*
Dannan's, as every node program's: the log's level and format, the io
threads, the drain's bound
.RB ( node.drain_ms ),
and the status lines.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/lir/config.yaml
The configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/lir/secrets.yaml
Settings that should not sit in the configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/lir
The node's state: its identity and Dannan's.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 once drained and stopped by a signal, 1 when the node could not run or a
second signal stopped it at once, 2 for a setting that cannot be used.
